---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Contribute — componentlib" description="How to add a component to componentlib.">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Contribute a component</h1>
    <p>
      Components live in the repository as plain files. Add a folder, open a pull
      request, and CI validates the schema and compiles every preview before merge.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="code-shell" aria-label="Contribution guide">
    <div class="code-panel">
      <div class="code-panel-inner">
        <pre><code>components/&lt;category&gt;/&lt;slug&gt;/
├── meta.json          # title, slug, category, tags, variants, preview
├── vanilla/
│   ├── index.html     # required: markup fragment
│   ├── style.css      # at least one of css/js required
│   └── script.js      # optional behavior
├── react/             # optional variant
│   ├── MyComponent.jsx
│   ├── style.css
│   └── demo.jsx       # imports './Component', mounts to #app
└── vue/               # optional variant
    ├── MyComponent.vue
    └── demo.js        # imports './Component.vue', mounts to #app</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" style="padding-block: 0 1rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.2rem;">Rules</h2>
    <ul style="color: var(--muted); max-width: 70ch;">
      <li>Slug and category are kebab-case and must match the folder names.</li>
      <li>Prefix your CSS classes (e.g. <code>ng-</code>) so snippets never collide when pasted together.</li>
      <li>Honor <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> in every animation.</li>
      <li>Interactive elements need keyboard access and visible focus styles.</li>
      <li>React/Vue demos import the component as <code>./Component</code> — the build resolves it to your file.</li>
      <li>Run <code>npm run validate</code> locally; it is the same gate CI runs.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
